  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Now that we have the avatar stats, it should be possible to identify and prove who crashed your instance by having the technical details. \n\nThis would also be easier by knowing who stood nearby while the game crashed. I can't believe how much \"Trusted Users\" just came to me right after I joined a world to crash me in the past for no reason. In fact, I trust the \"trusted users\" the least nowadays. And I feel completely unable to report them for their behaviour which gives me a horrible feeling.\n\nUnfortunately, I enabled the official partical limiter script (where I still can't believe this is not a default feature) way too late. I can't tell if it worked because I stopped joining crowded worlds because of that as well, but I still feel bad because I'm not able to report any of them when I'm not accidently recording my game 24/7.\n\nIn general, I recommend making the report function for users more usable by allowing to report other users after the game crashed - with providing a log file that has all the technical stats of each avatar during the crash and the relative position towards me. This would also be nice to have when the game hasn't fully crashed yet but is just not responsing. It could get triggered by pressing a key combination for example.",
